{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\051.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "R.H.S = (-2) + [(4)+ (-1))", "conf": 0.87, "box": [[207, 52], [584, 52], [584, 88], [207, 88]]}, {"text": "= (-2) + [(4) + (-1)", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[294, 111], [592, 108], [593, 146], [294, 150]]}, {"text": "= (-2) + [4 = 1]", "conf": 0.828, "box": [[293, 169], [549, 164], [550, 203], [294, 208]]}, {"text": "= (-2) + 3", "conf": 0.838, "box": [[291, 227], [452, 222], [453, 263], [293, 268]]}, {"text": "= +1", "conf": 0.749, "box": [[291, 282], [375, 282], [375, 321], [291, 321]]}, {"text": "So, L.H.S = R.H.S", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[204, 348], [460, 344], [460, 380], [205, 384]]}, {"text": "[(-2 + (+4)] + (-1) = (-2) + [(4 )+ (-1)]", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[204, 408], [789, 401], [789, 440], [205, 447]]}, {"text": "1=1", "conf": 0.72, "box": [[323, 475], [476, 475], [476, 506], [323, 506]]}, {"text": "Let's suppose a, b and c are any three integers, then: (a + b) + c= a + (b+ c)", "conf": 0.94, "box": [[195, 504], [1424, 491], [1425, 550], [196, 563]]}, {"text": "This is the generalised form of the Associative Law of integers under addition.", "conf": 0.92, "box": [[200, 580], [1414, 577], [1414, 623], [201, 626]]}, {"text": "d)Additive ldentity", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[201, 646], [577, 649], [577, 692], [200, 689]]}, {"text": "O is the called the additive identity because when we add O to any integer the result is the", "conf": 0.91, "box": [[196, 704], [1610, 711], [1610, 758], [195, 751]]}, {"text": "integer itself.", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[198, 769], [405, 769], [405, 809], [198, 809]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.825, "box": [[198, 828], [385, 828], [385, 869], [198, 869]]}, {"text": "If weadd 0 and +7, we get +7.", "conf": 0.845, "box": [[197, 884], [674, 889], [673, 925], [196, 921]]}, {"text": "0 + (+7) = 0 +7 = +7", "conf": 0.796, "box": [[312, 944], [645, 946], [644, 983], [312, 981]]}, {"text": "Example 2:", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[195, 1001], [379, 1003], [379, 1044], [194, 1042]]}, {"text": "If we add 0 and -5, we get -5.", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[194, 1059], [651, 1064], [650, 1100], [193, 1095]]}, {"text": "0 + (-5) = 0 -5 = -5", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[310, 1115], [614, 1120], [613, 1160], [309, 1154]]}, {"text": "e)Additivelnverse", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[200, 1169], [563, 1169], [563, 1205], [200, 1205]]}, {"text": "If the sum of two integers is zero (the additive identity), then both integers are called the", "conf": 0.934, "box": [[184, 1215], [1588, 1217], [1588, 1275], [184, 1273]]}, {"text": "additive inverse of each other.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[192, 1276], [685, 1283], [684, 1321], [191, 1315]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.867, "box": [[191, 1343], [379, 1343], [379, 1383], [191, 1383]]}, {"text": "If we add 3 and -3, we get 0.", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[191, 1395], [643, 1400], [642, 1439], [190, 1434]]}, {"text": "3+ (-3) = 3- 3 = 0", "conf": 0.809, "box": [[307, 1451], [608, 1454], [607, 1491], [307, 1488]]}, {"text": "here, 3 and -3 are the additive inverse of each other,", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[190, 1500], [1006, 1513], [1005, 1553], [189, 1539]]}, {"text": "Example2:", "conf": 0.812, "box": [[190, 1558], [379, 1558], [379, 1597], [190, 1597]]}, {"text": "If we add -4 and +4, we get0.", "conf": 0.837, "box": [[188, 1608], [659, 1614], [658, 1652], [187, 1647]]}, {"text": "-4+ (+4) = 4 +4 = 0", "conf": 0.847, "box": [[295, 1664], [637, 1667], [636, 1704], [295, 1701]]}, {"text": "here, -4 and +4 are the additive inverse of each other.", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[186, 1711], [1036, 1725], [1035, 1768], [185, 1754]]}, {"text": "and Distributiveproperty.", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[325, 1833], [661, 1841], [660, 1871], [325, 1862]]}, {"text": "https://www.mathgames.com/skill/3.37-properties-of-addition", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[324, 1869], [1136, 1888], [1135, 1921], [324, 1902]]}, {"text": "https://www.mathgames.com/skill/3.38-solve-using-praperties-of-addition", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[318, 1903], [130